{
  "an8.12:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.12 ",
  "an8.12:0.2": "2. The Great Chapter ",
  "an8.12:0.3": "With Sīha ",
  "an8.12:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "an8.12:1.2": "Now at that time several very prominent Licchavis were sitting together at the town hall, praising the Buddha, his teaching, and the Saṅgha in many ways. ",
  "an8.12:2.1": "Now at that time General Sīha, a disciple of the Jains, was sitting in that assembly. ",
  "an8.12:2.2": "He thought, ",
  "an8.12:2.3": "“That Blessed One must without a doubt be a perfected one, a fully awakened Buddha. For several very prominent Licchavis are praising the Buddha, his teaching, and the Saṅgha in many ways. ",
  "an8.12:2.4": "Why don’t I go to see that Blessed One, the perfected one, the fully awakened Buddha!” ",
  "an8.12:2.5": "Then General Sīha went to the Jain ascetic of the Ñātika clan and said to him, ",
  "an8.12:2.6": "“Sir, I’d like to go to see the ascetic Gotama.” ",
  "an8.12:3.1": "“But Sīha, you believe in the doctrine of action. Why should you go to see the ascetic Gotama, who teaches a doctrine of inaction? ",
  "an8.12:3.2": "For the ascetic Gotama believes in a doctrine of inaction, he teaches inaction, and he guides his disciples in that way.” ",
  "an8.12:3.3": "Then Sīha’s determination to go and see the Buddha died down. ",
